    <item>
      <title>El Niño Rains Paint the Atacama</title>
      <link>https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/el-nino-rains-paint-the-atacama/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/el-nino-rains-paint-the-atacama/</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://assets.science.nasa.gov/content/dam/science/esd/eo/images/iotd/2026/el-ni%C3%B1o-rains-paint-the-atacama/atacamabloom_oli2_20261024_th.jpg/jcr:content/renditions/cq5dam.web.1280.1280.jpeg" alt="El Niño Rains Paint the Atacama"&gt;&lt;p&gt;Winter precipitation helped wake dormant seeds in northern Chile, carpeting the desert with what may be the region’s most extensive flowering of the satellite era.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
